<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">18 October in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 18 October, from 1009 to 1922.</p></header>
<div class="tih-pinned-card"><p class="tih-pinned-label">International day</p><p class="tih-pinned-title">World Menopause Day</p><p class="tih-pinned-desc">Designated by the International Menopause Society and supported by the World Health Organisation, World Menopause Day raises awareness of the menopause and the support options available for improving health and wellbeing for the over one billion women worldwide who will reach this stage of life by 2025.</p></div>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/first-crusade" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/first-crusade.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1009 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,017 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Caliph al-Hakim has the Holy Sepulchre demolished</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On the orders of the Fatimid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> al-Hakim, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/church-of-the-holy-sepulchre">Church of the Holy Sepulchre</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> was torn down. Its destruction shocked Christendom and was remembered as a grievance when the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-crusade">First Crusade</a> was preached.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-crusade">First Crusade</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1685 CE <span class="tih-ago">341 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Louis XIV revokes the Edict of Nantes</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">By the Edict of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fontainebleau">Fontainebleau</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xiv">Louis XIV</a> outlawed Protestant worship in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. Some 200,000 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huguenots">Huguenots</a> fled abroad to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-republic">Dutch Republic</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a>, taking valuable skills with them.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/dutch-empire">Dutch Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-republic">Dutch Republic</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xiv">Louis XIV</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1767 CE <span class="tih-ago">259 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mason and Dixon complete their boundary survey</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Charles Mason and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jeremiah">Jeremiah</a> Dixon finished surveying the boundary between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pennsylvania">Pennsylvania</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maryland">Maryland</a>. Their line later became the symbolic divide between free and slave states.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1867 CE <span class="tih-ago">159 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The United States takes possession of Alaska</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sitka">Sitka</a>, the Russian flag was lowered and the US flag raised, formally transferring <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alaska">Alaska</a>, bought for 7.2 million dollars. Critics mocked the deal as 'Seward's Folly' until gold and oil proved its value.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alaska">Alaska</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1922 CE <span class="tih-ago">104 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The British Broadcasting Company is founded</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Wireless manufacturers formed the British Broadcasting Company to run <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>'s first national radio service. Under John Reith it became the public <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bbc">British Broadcasting Corporation</a> in 1927.</p></div></li></ol>
